# arm64: a fence behind two late stores of a new object. `fill` makes its objects in a loop by a constructor function that comes out of a variable, so the prototype is asked for at run time; where it is another than the site's, the structure is found in the table of transitions and stored in line, behind the fence of the fields. A fence of its own follows that store. x86-64 has no fence at all.
# f3 = fill
